        "11917": {"synopsis":"$7F - Character: copyright"},
        "11925": {"synopsis":"Unused: $00 up to $36B9."},
        "14010": {"synopsis":"Bytes nothing in this ROM reads, up to $37AD. Each byte XORed with $30 and with bit 7\ndropped gives, for most of them, a credits text: who did the test program, thanks, and the\nmachines and tools it was written with. Some bytes, mostly near the end, do not decode that\nway."},
        "14254": {"synopsis":"Unused: $00 up to $37EA."},
        "14315": {"synopsis":"MENU_LOADER's text for the lower screen (PRINT_BIT7_TEXT): AT 0,0, INK 0, PAPER 7, BRIGHT 0,\nthen \"Insert tape and press PLAY\", ENTER, \"To cancel - press BREAK twice\", its last letter\nwith bit 7 set."},
        "14380": {"synopsis":"Unused: $00 up to $3833."},
        "14388": {"synopsis":"The start-up copyright text, printed at $026E: the copyright sign, \"1982, 1986, 1987 Amstrad\nPlc.\", ENTER, the copyright sign, \"2000-2015 Garry Lancaster v1.43\", its last character with\nbit 7 set."},
        "14451": {"synopsis":"LINE_FIND's tests of the first line, moved here (by the JP at $15FB) to leave $15FE free: no\nline at all, no carry; the first line numbered BC or above, carry (Z when equal). Otherwise\non to LINE_FIND_LOOP; BC = 0 cannot get there, as every line is numbered 0 or above.","comment":"No lines: no carry"},
        "14452": {"comment":"The first line numbered BC or above?"},
        "14455": {"comment":"Yes: carry, Z when equal"},
        "14456": {"comment":"BC = 0?"},
        "14460": {"comment":"No: on through the program"},
        "14463": {"synopsis":"The I/O of a channel whose routines are at $5B00 (from $15FE, where ROM 3's PRINT_A_CHAN and\nINPUT_AD come back to after the $5B00 that swaps the ROMs):","comment":"DE = CURCHL"},
        "14464": {"comment":"HL = the offset of the word used"},
        "14467": {"comment":"C = it: 1 output, 3 input"},
        "14468": {"comment":"B = the character"},
        "14469": {"comment":"DE = the channel's letter"},
        "14474": {"comment":"A channel P?"},
        "14478": {"comment":"DE = the word at +$05"},
        "14479": {"comment":"Output?"},
        "14482": {"comment":"No: the word at +$07"},
        "14484": {"comment":"HL = the input routine"},
        "14489": {"comment":"Read through it"},
        "14491": {"synopsis":"Output: HL = the word at +$05, the output routine.","comment":"HL = the output routine"},
        "14496": {"comment":"Print through it"},
        "14498": {"synopsis":"A channel P: CHAN_P_OUT for output, CHAN_P_IN for input.","comment":"ROM 1's printer output"},
        "14501": {"comment":"Output?"},
        "14504": {"comment":"No: ROM 1's printer input"},
        "14507": {"synopsis":"Input through the routine at HL. When the word at ERR_SP is $107F (ROM 3's ED_ERROR, stacked\nwhile INPUT edits a line), the whole line is read here: the editor's frame is dropped (SP =\nERR_SP, ERR_SP = the word under it), and each character but ENTER is put into the line at\nK_CUR (ROM 3's $0F85, in INSERT_CHAR) until ENTER, which goes back to ROM 3 at $15FE.\nOtherwise one read (CHAN_X_IN_ONE). A routine returns carry and the character, Z for none\nyet (tried again), or neither for the end of the data (error 7, CHAN_X_EOF).","comment":"TV_FLAG bit 3 cleared"},
        "14511": {"comment":"The routine kept"},
        "14512": {"comment":"DE = the word at ERR_SP"},
        "14518": {"comment":"Is it $107F, ROM 3's ED_ERROR?"},
        "14524": {"comment":"HL = the routine"},
        "14525": {"comment":"No: a single read"},
        "14527": {"comment":"Yes: the stack from ERR_SP"},
        "14531": {"comment":"The $107F dropped"},
        "14532": {"comment":"ERR_SP = the word under it"},
        "14537": {"comment":"IX kept"},
        "14539": {"synopsis":"One character of the line read through the routine, which returns to $38D1.","comment":"The routine kept"},
        "14540": {"comment":"Its return: $38D1"},
        "14544": {"comment":"Read a character"},
        "14545": {"comment":"Carry: one read?"},
        "14547": {"comment":"Z: none yet?"},
        "14549": {"synopsis":"The end of the data: error 7 (report 8) through IO_REPORT. Also from $0332, $0348 and $08B4,\nand from the channel V routines.","comment":"Error 7"},
        "14553": {"synopsis":"No character yet: the routine tried again.","comment":"HL = the routine"},
        "14556": {"synopsis":"A character: ENTER ends the line; any other is put into it.","comment":"ENTER?"},
        "14560": {"comment":"$5B5A kept: RST $28 uses it"},
        "14564": {"comment":"ROM 3's $0F85: A put in at K_CUR"},
        "14567": {"comment":"$5B5A back"},
        "14571": {"comment":"HL = the routine"},
        "14572": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "14574": {"synopsis":"ENTER: back to ROM 3 at $15FE with A = 13, through the ROM swap at $5B00.","comment":"The routine dropped"},
        "14575": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "14577": {"comment":"ROM 3's $15FE as the return"},
        "14581": {"comment":"The ROMs swapped: on in ROM 3"},
        "14584": {"synopsis":"One read through the routine; back to ROM 3 at $15FE with carry (a character) or Z (none),\notherwise error 7.","comment":"ROM 3's $15FE as the return"},
        "14588": {"comment":"Read a character"},
        "14591": {"comment":"Carry: one read, back to ROM 3"},
        "14594": {"comment":"Z: none, back to ROM 3"},
        "14597": {"comment":"Neither: the end of the data"},
        "14599": {"synopsis":"Output: the character (B) printed through the routine at HL, IX kept, then back to ROM 3 at\n$15FE through the ROM swap at $5B00.","comment":"ROM 3's $15FE as the return"},
        "14603": {"comment":"A = the character"},
        "14604": {"comment":"IX kept"},
        "14606": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "14611": {"comment":"The ROMs swapped: on in ROM 3"},
        "14614": {"synopsis":"Jumps to HL.","comment":"Jump to the routine"},
        "14615": {"synopsis":"Gives error A through ROM 3's ERROR_L (L = A), with X_PTR = CH_ADD. From CHAN_X_EOF (7,\nreport 8), CHAN_BAD_IO and $3EEF ($12, report J).","comment":"X_PTR = CH_ADD"},
        "14621": {"comment":"L = the error"},
        "14622": {"comment":"ROM 3's ERROR_L"},
        "14625": {"synopsis":"A channel P's output: ROM 1's routine at $1F6E, through CALL_ROM1.","comment":"ROM 1's printer output"},
        "14631": {"synopsis":"A channel P's input: ROM 1's routine at $1E70, through CALL_ROM1.","comment":"ROM 1's printer input"},
        "14637": {"synopsis":"The I/O of the current channel for ROM 2 (its ROM0_392D_0, _2 and _4, through CALL_ROM0),\nwith the caller's registers in the other set (not for DE = 2):","comment":"HL = the channel"},
        "14640": {"comment":"Its output routine $5B00?"},
        "14645": {"comment":"High byte"},
        "14648": {"comment":"$5B?"},
        "14652": {"comment":"HL = the channel's letter"},
        "14658": {"comment":"A channel P?"},
        "14662": {"comment":"Yes: the position operation?"},
        "14665": {"comment":"Not for P: error $12"},
        "14667": {"comment":"Input?"},
        "14669": {"comment":"Yes: ROM 1's printer input"},
        "14672": {"comment":"Output: A = the caller's C"},
        "14674": {"comment":"ROM 1's printer output"},
        "14677": {"synopsis":"A channel with routines at $5B00: DE = the word at +$05 + DE, the routine.","comment":"A = 0, 2 or 4"},
        "14678": {"comment":"DE = the word at +$05 + DE"},
        "14682": {"comment":"The routine to go to"},
        "14683": {"comment":"Input?"},
        "14687": {"comment":"No: the caller's registers"},
        "14688": {"comment":"A = their C"},
        "14689": {"comment":"Go to the routine"},
        "14690": {"synopsis":"Input: the routine run with CHAN_IO_AGAIN as its return.","comment":"Its return: CHAN_IO_AGAIN"},
        "14694": {"comment":"Read a character"},
        "14695": {"synopsis":"A channel of ROM 3's kind: its output (DE = 0) or input routine (DE = 2) run in ROM 3\nthrough CALL_ROM3_GO, which takes the stacked $5B5A as HL for the routine.","comment":"The position operation?"},
        "14698": {"comment":"Not here: error $12"},
        "14700": {"comment":"DE = the word at +0 or +2"},
        "14704": {"comment":"$5B5A on the stack: HL for it"},
        "14708": {"comment":"Input?"},
        "14712": {"comment":"Output: back to CHAN_IO_OUT_END"},
        "14718": {"comment":"HL = the routine"},
        "14719": {"comment":"A = the caller's C"},
        "14722": {"comment":"Run in ROM 3"},
        "14725": {"synopsis":"Back from ROM 3's output routine: $5B5A from HL (the value it was given).","comment":"$5B5A back"},
        "14729": {"synopsis":"Input: the routine run in ROM 3, back to CHAN_IO_IN_END.","comment":"Back to CHAN_IO_IN_END"},
        "14735": {"comment":"HL = the routine"},
        "14736": {"comment":"Run in ROM 3"},
        "14739": {"synopsis":"Back from ROM 3's input routine: $5B5A from HL (the value it was given).","comment":"$5B5A back"},
        "14742": {"synopsis":"Input done: carry, a character; otherwise the input tried again.","comment":"A character read?"},
        "14743": {"comment":"No: input again"},
        "14748": {"synopsis":"Error $12 (report J) through IO_REPORT: an operation the channel cannot do. W_CHAN_TEMPL (in\nROM 2) gives this address as a channel W's input and position routines.","comment":"Error $12"},
        "14753": {"synopsis":"Finds the string array of the current channel V (the letter, bit 7 set, at +$0D): VARS\nsearched for it (ROM 3's NEXT_ITEM); none, or not of one dimension, error $12 (CHAN_BAD_IO).","comment":"HL = the channel's +$0D"},
        "14760": {"comment":"A = the array's letter"},
        "14761": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "14762": {"comment":"HL = VARS"},
        "14765": {"comment":"C = the letter"},
        "14766": {"synopsis":"One variable: the end marker, the array, or the next.","comment":"The variables' end?"},
        "14769": {"comment":"Yes: error $12"},
        "14771": {"comment":"The letter?"},
        "14774": {"comment":"No: the next variable"},
        "14779": {"comment":"HL = it"},
        "14782": {"synopsis":"The array: one dimension, its length and first character; the position.","comment":"HL = its number of dimensions"},
        "14785": {"comment":"A = it"},
        "14787": {"comment":"Not 1: error $12"},
        "14790": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "14794": {"comment":"DE = the first character"},
        "14795": {"comment":"HL = the channel's +$0D"},
        "14796": {"comment":"HL = the position, at +$0E"},
        "14801": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "14802": {"comment":"Inside the array: carry"},
        "14807": {"synopsis":"A channel V's input (the second word of V_CHAN_TEMPL): A = the character at the position,\nand the position one on; past the end, error 7 (CHAN_X_EOF).","comment":"Find the array; inside it?"},
        "14810": {"comment":"No: error 7"},
        "14813": {"comment":"A = the character"},
        "14815": {"synopsis":"The position (the word at +$0E) one on; carry set.","comment":"HL = the channel's +$0E"},
        "14822": {"comment":"DE = the position"},
        "14825": {"comment":"One on"},
        "14829": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "14831": {"synopsis":"A channel V's output (the first word of V_CHAN_TEMPL): A put at the position, and the\nposition one on; past the end, error 7 (CHAN_X_EOF).","comment":"The character kept"},
        "14832": {"comment":"Find the array; inside it?"},
        "14835": {"comment":"No: error 7"},
        "14838": {"comment":"HL = the place"},
        "14840": {"comment":"The character stored"},
        "14841": {"comment":"The position one on"},
        "14843": {"synopsis":"A channel V's position operation (the third word of V_CHAN_TEMPL), by B: 0 gives the\nposition in DE:HL; 1 sets it from DE:HL (DE must be 0 and HL less than the length, otherwise\nerror 7); 2 or more gives the length in DE:HL.","comment":"The new position kept"},
        "14845": {"comment":"A = the operation"},
        "14847": {"comment":"Find the array"},
        "14850": {"comment":"0: the position?"},
        "14854": {"comment":"Yes: the stacked words dropped"},
        "14856": {"comment":"DE:HL = the position"},
        "14860": {"synopsis":"1 sets the position; 2 and up give the length (VCH_PTR_LEN).","comment":"1: set it?"},
        "14863": {"comment":"Yes: HL = the high word"},
        "14864": {"comment":"Not 0?"},
        "14866": {"comment":"Yes: error 7"},
        "14869": {"comment":"HL = the new position"},
        "14870": {"comment":"At or past the length?"},
        "14873": {"comment":"Yes: error 7"},
        "14876": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "14877": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "14878": {"comment":"HL = the channel's +$0E"},
        "14885": {"comment":"The position stored"},
        "14889": {"synopsis":"2 or more: DE:HL = the array's length.","comment":"The stacked words dropped"},
        "14891": {"comment":"HL = the length"},
        "14893": {"comment":"DE = 0"},
        "14897": {"synopsis":"Unused: $00 up to $3DFF."},
        "15872": {"synopsis":"ROM 2's CALL_ROM0, of which these are the same bytes: it parks AF and HL at $5B56 and\n$5B52, reads the word after the CALL into HL (stepping the return address past it) and\nclears bit 2 of port $1FFD (and $5B67) with interrupts off. That OUT, at $3E1C, pages this\nROM in, so the code goes on here at $3E1E: CALL_ROM0_BACK is pushed as the return, AF and\nHL are restored and the RET jumps to the address. Nothing in this ROM calls it.","comment":"HL parked"},
        "15875": {"comment":"AF parked"},
        "15877": {"comment":"At $5B56"},
        "15880": {"comment":"The word after the CALL"},
        "15881": {"comment":"BC = the address"},
        "15885": {"comment":"Return address stepped past it"},
        "15886": {"comment":"HL = the address"},
        "15888": {"comment":"Bit 2 of port $1FFD cleared: ROM 0"},
        "15894": {"comment":"Bit 2 cleared"},
        "15897": {"comment":"Copy and port, no interrupts"},
        "15900": {"comment":"ROM 0 in: on at $3E1E here"},
        "15902": {"comment":"From here in this ROM"},
        "15903": {"comment":"The way back first"},
        "15907": {"comment":"Then the address"},
        "15908": {"comment":"AF and HL back"},
        "15912": {"comment":"AF from $5B56"},
        "15913": {"comment":"HL from $5B52"},
        "15916": {"comment":"To the address"},
        "15917": {"synopsis":"Where a routine called through CALL_ROM0 returns: bit 2 of port $1FFD (and $5B67) set\nagain with interrupts off, keeping AF and BC; after the OUT at $3E3B the code goes on in ROM\n2's copy.","comment":"BC and AF kept"},
        "15919": {"comment":"Bit 2 of port $1FFD set: ROM 2"},
        "15925": {"comment":"Bit 2 set"},
        "15928": {"comment":"Copy and port, no interrupts"},
        "15931": {"comment":"ROM 2 in: on at $3E3D there"},
        "15933": {"comment":"From here in ROM 2"},
        "15934": {"comment":"AF and BC back"},
        "15937": {"synopsis":"For a channel F: B = its file number (+$0D), then RAM bank 7 and the other stack\n(BANK7_STACK), and back to the caller, whose return address is taken off the stack first.","comment":"HL = the channel's +$0D"},
        "15944": {"comment":"B = the file number"},
        "15945": {"comment":"HL = the return address"},
        "15946": {"comment":"Bank 7 and the other stack"},
        "15949": {"comment":"Back to the caller"},
        "15950": {"synopsis":"A channel F's position operation (the third word of F_CHAN_TEMPL in ROM 2), by B, through\n+3DOS (CALL_ROM2): 0 gives the file's position in DE:HL (FILE_POS_GET), 1 sets it from E:HL\n(FILE_POS_SET), 2 or more gives its length in DE:HL (FILE_LEN_GET). Failure: error $12\n(FCH_DONE).","comment":"The other set"},
        "15951": {"comment":"B = the file number, bank 7"},
        "15954": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "15955": {"comment":"The caller's registers"},
        "15956": {"comment":"A = the operation"},
        "15957": {"comment":"B = the file number"},
        "15958": {"comment":"0: the position?"},
        "15961": {"comment":"1: set it?"},
        "15964": {"comment":"2 and up: the file's length"},
        "15969": {"comment":"D = 0, then done"},
        "15971": {"synopsis":"0: the file's position (FILE_POS_GET), D = 0.","comment":"The file's position"},
        "15976": {"synopsis":"D = 0: the 24-bit E:HL as DE:HL.","comment":"D = 0"},
        "15978": {"comment":"Done"},
        "15980": {"synopsis":"1: the file's position set from E:HL (FILE_POS_SET).","comment":"The position set"},
        "15985": {"comment":"Done"},
        "15987": {"synopsis":"A channel F's input (the second word of F_CHAN_TEMPL in ROM 2): a byte read from the file\n(+3DOS FILE_READ_BYTE, through CALL_ROM2) into A. Failure: error $12 (FCH_DONE).","comment":"B = the file number, bank 7"},
        "15990": {"comment":"A byte read"},
        "15995": {"comment":"A = it"},
        "15996": {"comment":"Done"},
        "15998": {"synopsis":"Unused: two bytes $00."},
        "16000": {"synopsis":"Calls the address in the word after the CALL in ROM 1, keeping AF, BC and HL (parked at\n$5B56, $5B54 and $5B52): the word is read into HL and the return address stepped past it;\nbit 4 of the paging byte $5B5C (port $7FFD) is set with interrupts off, which pages ROM 1\nin, and the code goes on at $3EA2 in ROM 1's copy; CALL_ROM1_BACK is pushed as the return,\nAF, BC and HL are restored and the RET jumps to the address. The return runs ROM 1's\n$3EB5, which clears the bit again. ROM 1 has the same routine here with the bit cleared,\nfor its calls into this ROM. Called at $0285, $08E2, $0911, $092B, $0D94 and $210E.","comment":"HL parked"},
        "16003": {"comment":"BC parked"},
        "16007": {"comment":"AF parked"},
        "16009": {"comment":"At $5B56"},
        "16012": {"comment":"The word after the CALL"},
        "16013": {"comment":"BC = the address"},
        "16017": {"comment":"Return address stepped past it"},
        "16018": {"comment":"HL = the address"},
        "16020": {"comment":"Bit 4 of port $7FFD set: ROM 1"},
        "16023": {"comment":"Bit 4 set"},
        "16026": {"comment":"Copy and port, no interrupts"},
        "16032": {"comment":"ROM 1 in: on at $3EA2 there"},
        "16034": {"comment":"From here in ROM 1"},
        "16035": {"comment":"The way back first"},
        "16039": {"comment":"Then the address"},
        "16040": {"comment":"AF, BC and HL back"},
        "16044": {"comment":"AF from $5B56"},
        "16045": {"comment":"BC from $5B54"},
        "16049": {"comment":"HL from $5B52"},
        "16052": {"comment":"To the address"},
        "16053": {"synopsis":"Where a routine of this ROM called through ROM 1's copy of CALL_ROM1 returns: bit 4 of\n$5B5C (port $7FFD) set again with interrupts off, which pages ROM 1 back in, keeping AF and\nBC; the code after the OUT at $3EC3 runs in ROM 1.","comment":"AF and BC kept"},
        "16055": {"comment":"Bit 4 of port $7FFD set: ROM 1"},
        "16058": {"comment":"Bit 4 set"},
        "16061": {"comment":"Copy and port, no interrupts"},
        "16067": {"comment":"ROM 1 in: on at $3EC5 there"},
        "16069": {"comment":"From here in ROM 1"},
        "16070": {"comment":"BC and AF back"},
        "16073": {"synopsis":"This ROM's own call into ROM 2 (+3DOS), from the channel F routines: the address in the word\nafter the CALL called in ROM 2, keeping AF, BC and HL (parked at $5B56, $5B54 and $5B52),\nwith CALL_ROM2_BACK0 as the way back; the paging is CALL_ROM2_GO's.","comment":"HL parked"},
        "16076": {"comment":"BC parked"},
        "16080": {"comment":"AF parked"},
        "16082": {"comment":"At $5B56"},
        "16085": {"comment":"The word after the CALL"},
        "16086": {"comment":"BC = the address"},
        "16090": {"comment":"Return address stepped past it"},
        "16091": {"comment":"The way back: CALL_ROM2_BACK0"},
        "16094": {"comment":"On at CALL_ROM2_GO"},
        "16096": {"synopsis":"A channel F's output (the first word of F_CHAN_TEMPL in ROM 2): the byte in A written to the\nfile (+3DOS FILE_WRITE_BYTE, through CALL_ROM2). Failure: error $12 (FCH_DONE).","comment":"C = the byte"},
        "16097": {"comment":"B = the file number, bank 7"},
        "16100": {"comment":"The byte written"},
        "16105": {"synopsis":"The end of a channel F routine: bank 0 and the stack back (BANK0_STACK); +3DOS's carry,\nsuccess, returns; no carry gives error $12 (report J) through IO_REPORT.","comment":"Bank 0 and the stack back"},
        "16108": {"comment":"Success: done"},
        "16109": {"comment":"Failure: error $12"},
        "16128": {"synopsis":"ROM 1's CALL_ROM2, of which these are the same bytes, and of which this ROM runs the middle:\nROM 1 parks HL, BC and AF at $5B52, $5B54 and $5B56, reads the word after the CALL and, with\nCALL_ROM2_BACK as the way back, goes on at CALL_ROM2_GO, whose clearing of bit 4 of port\n$7FFD (at $3F24) pages this ROM in.","comment":"HL parked"},
        "16131": {"comment":"BC parked"},
        "16135": {"comment":"AF parked"},
        "16137": {"comment":"At $5B56"},
        "16140": {"comment":"The word after the CALL"},
        "16141": {"comment":"BC = the address"},
        "16145": {"comment":"Return address stepped past it"},
        "16146": {"comment":"The way back: CALL_ROM2_BACK"},
        "16149": {"synopsis":"The rest of CALL_ROM2 and ROM1_CALL_ROM2: the way back (HL) stacked, bit 4 of port $7FFD\ncleared (from ROM 1 this pages ROM 0 in), then bit 2 of port $1FFD set, which pages ROM 2\nin, and on in ROM 2's copy of these bytes at the address with AF, BC and HL back.","comment":"The way back stacked"},
        "16150": {"comment":"HL = the address"},
        "16152": {"comment":"Bit 4 of port $7FFD cleared: ROM 0"},
        "16155": {"comment":"Bit 4 cleared"},
        "16158": {"comment":"Copy and port, no interrupts"},
        "16164": {"comment":"ROM 0 in: on at $3F26 here"},
        "16166": {"comment":"From here in this ROM: bit 2 of $1FFD set"},
        "16169": {"comment":"Bit 2 set"},
        "16174": {"comment":"Port $1FFD"},
        "16177": {"comment":"ROM 2 in: on at $3F33 there"},
        "16179": {"comment":"From here in ROM 2"},
        "16180": {"comment":"Then the address"},
        "16181": {"comment":"AF, BC and HL back"},
        "16185": {"comment":"AF from $5B56"},
        "16186": {"comment":"BC from $5B54"},
        "16190": {"comment":"HL from $5B52"},
        "16193": {"comment":"To the address"},
        "16194": {"synopsis":"The way back from ROM 2 to ROM 1, keeping AF and BC: ROM 2 clears bit 2 of port $1FFD (and\n$5B67), which pages this ROM in, so $3F52-$3F5D run here and set bit 4 of port $7FFD (and\n$5B5C), which pages ROM 1 back in for the RET.","comment":"BC and AF kept"},
        "16196": {"comment":"Bit 2 of port $1FFD cleared: ROM 0"},
        "16199": {"comment":"Bit 2 cleared"},
        "16202": {"comment":"Copy and port, no interrupts"},
        "16208": {"comment":"ROM 0 in: on at $3F52 here"},
        "16210": {"comment":"From here in this ROM: bit 4 set"},
        "16213": {"comment":"Bit 4 set"},
        "16218": {"comment":"Port $7FFD"},
        "16221": {"comment":"ROM 1 in: on at $3F5F there"},
        "16223": {"comment":"From here in ROM 1"},
        "16224": {"comment":"AF and BC back"},
        "16227": {"synopsis":"The way back to this ROM from a routine called through CALL_ROM2 (run in ROM 2's copy of\nthese bytes): bit 2 of port $1FFD (and $5B67) cleared, which pages ROM 0 back in, keeping AF\nand BC; the code after the OUT at $3F71 runs here.","comment":"BC and AF kept"},
        "16229": {"comment":"Bit 2 of port $1FFD cleared"},
        "16234": {"comment":"Copy and port, no interrupts"},
        "16241": {"comment":"ROM 0 in: on at $3F73 here"},
        "16243": {"comment":"From here in this ROM"},
        "16244": {"comment":"AF and BC back"},
        "16247": {"synopsis":"Removes BC bytes at HL (a channel being closed) from CHANS, for ROM 2's SCLOSE_RECLAIM\n(through CALL_ROM0, with HL and BC in the other set): ROM 3's RECLAIM, $5B5A kept, then\nevery stream word (19 of them, from STRMS) above the channel's offset from CHANS made BC\nsmaller.","comment":"HL = the place, BC = the length"},
        "16248": {"synopsis":"CHANS_RECLAIM entered with HL and BC in this set: from $2450, which takes BC bytes out of a\nchannel W's buffer.","comment":"The place and length kept"},
        "16250": {"comment":"$5B5A on the stack, HL back"},
        "16255": {"comment":"ROM 3's RECLAIM"},
        "16258": {"comment":"$5B5A back"},
        "16262": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "16263": {"comment":"HL = the place"},
        "16264": {"comment":"Its offset from CHANS"},
        "16271": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "16272": {"comment":"19 streams"},
        "16274": {"comment":"From STRMS"},
        "16277": {"synopsis":"One stream word: made BC smaller when it is above the offset.","comment":"DE = the stream's word"},
        "16280": {"comment":"HL = the offset"},
        "16281": {"comment":"The offset below the word?"},
        "16285": {"comment":"No: as it is"},
        "16287": {"comment":"Yes: the word BC smaller"},
        "16292": {"synopsis":"The word stored back; the next stream.","comment":"HL = the stream's place"},
        "16293": {"comment":"Stored back"},
        "16298": {"comment":"The next stream"},
        "16301": {"comment":"The offset dropped"},
        "16303": {"synopsis":"Makes room for BC bytes at HL in CHANS (a channel being opened), for ROM 2's CHAN_NEW\n(through CALL_ROM0, with HL and BC in the other set): ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM, $5B5A kept; DATADD,\nwhen now below PROG - 1, set to PROG - 1; then every stream word (19 of them, from STRMS)\nabove the place's offset from CHANS made BC larger.","comment":"HL = the place, BC = the length"},
        "16304": {"synopsis":"CHANS_MAKE_ROOM entered with HL and BC in this set: from $23F5, which makes a channel W's\nbuffer BC bytes larger.","comment":"The place and length kept"},
        "16306": {"comment":"$5B5A on the stack, HL back"},
        "16311": {"comment":"ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM"},
        "16314": {"comment":"$5B5A back"},
        "16318": {"comment":"DATADD below PROG - 1?"},
        "16331": {"comment":"Yes: DATADD = PROG - 1"},
        "16335": {"synopsis":"The streams: their offsets from CHANS compared with the place's.","comment":"BC = the length"},
        "16336": {"comment":"HL = the place"},
        "16337": {"comment":"Its offset from CHANS"},
        "16344": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "16345": {"comment":"19 streams"},
        "16347": {"comment":"From STRMS"},
        "16350": {"synopsis":"One stream word: made BC larger when it is above the offset.","comment":"DE = the stream's word"},
        "16353": {"comment":"HL = the offset"},
        "16354": {"comment":"The offset below the word?"},
        "16358": {"comment":"No: as it is"},
        "16360": {"comment":"Yes: the word BC larger"},
        "16364": {"synopsis":"The word stored back; the next stream.","comment":"HL = the stream's place"},
        "16365": {"comment":"Stored back"},
        "16370": {"comment":"The next stream"},
        "16373": {"comment":"The offset dropped"},
        "16375": {"synopsis":"ROM 2's way into this ROM: its SHOW_MESSAGE calls $3FF7 through CALL_ROM0. It jumps to\n$2187, which takes the zero flag, A and HL as ROM 2 passes them.","comment":"On at $2187"},
        "16378": {"synopsis":"Unused: $00 up to the last byte."}
      }
    }
